cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jaxglobal in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "jaxglobal: deterministic global optimization of plain JAX functions"
abstract: >-
  jaxglobal is a deterministic global optimizer for continuous and
  mixed-integer nonlinear problems written as plain JAX functions. It traces
  the objective and constraints to a jaxpr and re-interprets every primitive
  as McCormick and alphaBB relaxations, which are jit-compiled and vmapped
  over boxes in a batched spatial branch-and-bound. It returns a feasible
  point and a proven lower bound, and reads AMPL .nl models.
type: software
